From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 04:07:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] donate: crypto donation page in the web UI + README
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a Donate page to the rnsbox-portal admin UI (sidebar menu entry + a
footer link on every authenticated page) showing five crypto wallets
(BTC/ETH/SOL/LTC/DOGE), each with a static QR code, the full address, a
copy button and an open-in-wallet link.

- donate.py holds the addresses (single source of truth); app.py serves
  /donate (endpoint pinned so url_for('donate') stays valid alongside the
  module import); donate.html + style.css render the page; base.html gains
  the menu entry and a site footer.
- QR codes are pre-generated static SVGs (static/qr/*.svg, bare address so
  scan == copy == shown) — no runtime QR dependency, works fully offline.
  The copy button falls back to execCommand since the LAN portal is plain
  HTTP (clipboard API is secure-context only).
- rnsbox-portal.mk installs the new static/qr/ subdir (the old static/*
  glob would choke on a subdirectory).
- README.RNSBox.md gains a Support section with the same addresses.

Addresses are checksum-verified (bech32 BTC/LTC, base58check DOGE,
32-byte ed25519 SOL, hex ETH).
